From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local-hotfix <local-hotfix@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix false-positive .NET installs for Unity/Mono games

The dependency-installer only gated Mono detection for dotnet48 and
dotnet35sp1. That allowed dotnet472 / dotnet40 / dotnet20 to be
requested for games that already ship their own Mono runtime, which
later caused winetricks to fail or leave the prefix in a broken state.

Include all .NET Framework verbs in the Mono gate so Unity/Mono games
stop triggering unnecessary .NET installations.
---
 dependency-installer/dependency-installer | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dependency-installer/dependency-installer b/dependency-installer/dependency-installer
index 2d85afa..9a99b9d 100755
--- a/dependency-installer/dependency-installer
+++ b/dependency-installer/dependency-installer
@@ -559,7 +559,7 @@
         if dep.get("skip_if_wine"):
             continue
 
-        # If game ships with Mono, skip .NET detection (Mono handles it)
-        if dep["id"] in ("dotnet48", "dotnet35sp1"):
+        # If game ships with Mono, skip .NET detection (Mono handles it).
+        # All .NET Framework verbs must be gated here, not only a subset,
+        # otherwise Unity/Mono games trigger false-positive dotnet installs
+        # that later fail or corrupt the prefix.
+        if dep["id"] in ("dotnet48", "dotnet472", "dotnet40", "dotnet35sp1", "dotnet20"):
             has_mono = False
             has_dotnet = False
